                    <msContents>
                        <summary>Three treatises relating to the Wahhābi sect: 1. a letter written
                            by Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb (ff. 1b-11b); 2. an anonymous treatise
                            confirming the opinion of Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb on the right kind
                            of prayer and invocation (ff. 12b-19b); 3. a refutation of the Wahhābi
                            tenets by Muḥammad Abu al-Saʿud al-Sharwāni (ff. 2b-79b).</summary>

                        <msItem xml:id="manuscript_14318-item1">
                            <locus from="1b" to="11b">1b-11b</locus>
                            <title xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc" key="">Al-Risalah al-Madaniyah fī
                                maʿrifat bahāʾi al-uluhiyyah</title>
                            <title xml:lang="ar" type="alt">الرسالة المدنية فى معرفة بهاء
                                الالهية</title>
                            <title xml:lang="en" type="alt">The Madīnite Epistle concerning the
                                knowledge of the beauty of the Divinity</title>
                            <author key="person_88344566"><persName xml:lang="en">Muḥammad ibn ʻAbd
                                    al-Wahhāb, 1703 or 1704-1792</persName>
                                <persName xml:lang="ar">محمد بن عبد الوهاب</persName></author>

                            <textLang mainLang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                            <note><p>The letter was written and sent to Madinah by Muḥammad b. ʿAbd
                                    al-Wahhāb, the head of the Wahhābi movement. The author
                                    demonstrates the transcending power of God in connection with
                                    all created human beings, and shows that prayer must primarily
                                    be addressed direct to Him.</p>
                            </note>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="manuscript_14318-item2">
                            <locus from="12b" to="19b">12b-19b</locus>
                            <title xml:lang="en" key="">Treatise on Wahhābi theology</title>
                            <note><p>Treatise confirming the opinion of Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb
                                    on the right kind of prayer and invocation. The unknown author
                                    contends that prayer should be addressed to God alone, either
                                    directly or indirectly through the name of the Prophet and
                                    dwells on some other points of Wahhābi doctrines, especially
                                    sepulchral constructions.</p></note>
                            <textLang mainLang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="manuscript_14318-item3">
                            <locus from="20b" to="79b">20b-79b</locus>
                            <title xml:lang="en" key="">Treatise on Wahhābi theology</title>
                            <author key=""><persName xml:lang="en">Muḥammad Abū al-Saʿūd al-Shirwānī
                                    al-Madanī</persName><persName xml:lang="ar">محمد ابو السعود
                                    الشروانى المدنى</persName></author>
                            <note><p>Lengthy refutation of the Wahhābi tenets. The words introducing
                                    a refuted sentence are <quote>واما قولك</quote>, written in red. </p>
                                <p>The colophon on (79a-79b) states that the author composed this
                                    treatise in 1211 AH (1796 CE), and that the present manuscript
                                    was transcribed nine years later, in 1220 AH (1805 CE).</p>
                                <p>Clear copy apart from one marginal note on <locus from="49a"
                                        >folio 49a</locus>.</p></note>
                            <colophon>وقد تم تبييضها على يد الفقير … محمد الى السعود الشروانى المدنى
                                الحنفى … وذلك فى اواخر شهر رجب الفرد من عام الظفر ١٢١١ ختم بخير بجاه
                                سيد البشره. قد تم هذه الرسالة على يد كاتبه الفقير اسحق من قضاة
                                الديار المصرية فى سنة عشرين ومائتان والف من هجرة من له العز
                                والشرف</colophon>
                            <textLang mainLang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                        </msItem>
                    </msContents>
